      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T23:24:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "when `SetString` runs `self._do` inside `BatchWrites` (eg updating an existing key), `_SaveJson` is deferred so `_cache_fingerprint` stays stale. if `_batch_ops` is empty on the next `SetString`, this check mismatches and triggers ClearCache and an extra git subprocess\n\ncould we drop _file_stat / _StatFile and track `_cache_fingerprint` everywhere (refreshing it after direct `_do()` writes and check it against `existing` in _TryWriteBatchLocked)?",
      "revId": "4c6a02b7df70d80dbff21851ee5c618b1ec2f033",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
